<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak parlt amends, then approves securities law.</title>
<headline>Slovak parlt amends, then approves securities law.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Slovak parliament on Tuesday approved a new securities law forcing trading of registered shares onto accredited bourses.</p>
<p>But the law, which had been sent back to parliament by President Michal Kovac for revision, omitted a controversial clause which would have allowed major shareholders to arbitrarily cancel trading of an issue.</p>
</text>
